# Git identity map — P2P Trust Stack
#
# One contributor had two GitHub identities configured on different machines.
# Commits authored as `shannon@iotinventor.com` are the same person as
# `simmunity@gmail.com`. Resolving both to one identity keeps attribution and
# copyright audits correct WITHOUT rewriting history (which would change every
# commit hash).
#
# Check with: git check-mailmap <shannon@iotinventor.com>
